---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '@/components/nav/NavBar.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/nav/Footer.astro';
import Container from '@/components/layout/Container.astro';
import Section from '@/components/layout/Section.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | KourtQ"
  description="Privacy Policy for KourtQ pickleball scoring app by NekoCode"
>
  <NavBar slot="header" />

  <Section size="lg" class="legal-page">
    <Container size="narrow">
      <a href={`${base}apps`} class="back-link">Back to apps</a>

      <div class="legal-header glass-panel">
        <span class="legal-icon" aria-hidden="true">Privacy</span>
        <div>
          <h1 class="text-title-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="legal-subtitle">KourtQ by NekoCode</p>
        </div>
        <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: June 26, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content glass-panel">
        <div class="highlight-box primary">
          <h3>Local-first scorekeeping</h3>
          <p>
            KourtQ is built for local pickleball scoring. No account is required, KourtQ does not run a
            NekoCode cloud sync backend, and match data is designed to stay on the device unless you choose to
            share or export it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <section>
          <h2>Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how KourtQ ("we," "our," or "us") handles information when you use
            the KourtQ iOS app and Apple Watch companion experience.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information KourtQ Processes</h2>
          <p>KourtQ may process information you enter or generate while scoring, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Player names, team assignments, and local player profile details</li>
            <li>Match setup choices, scoring rules, serve state, rally actions, and game results</li>
            <li>Local match history, score summaries, and app preferences</li>
            <li>Apple Watch companion state needed to mirror scoring controls from the paired iPhone</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Where Data Is Stored</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>KourtQ stores scoring data locally on your device</li>
            <li>No NekoCode account is required for the core scoring flow</li>
            <li>We do not upload your match history, player list, or scoring data to a NekoCode cloud backend</li>
            <li>The Apple Watch companion uses paired-device communication to show and send scoring state</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
          <p>Data may leave your device only in limited cases:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>If you use a device share sheet, export feature, screenshot, or support message</li>
            <li>If you open external support, website, App Store, or system links</li>
            <li>If Apple processes diagnostics, crash reports, store analytics, or app distribution data under Apple policies</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Analytics and Advertising</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>KourtQ does not include a third-party advertising SDK in the current iOS app</li>
            <li>KourtQ does not require third-party analytics for the core scoring flow</li>
            <li>Apple may provide App Store and device diagnostics data according to your device and Apple account settings</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Permissions</h2>
          <p>
            KourtQ may use network access for app resources, support links, store services, or platform features.
            The Apple Watch companion uses Apple system frameworks for paired-device score controls. KourtQ does
            not require location, camera, microphone, or contacts access for core scorekeeping.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Local data stays on your device until you delete it, clear app data, or uninstall KourtQ</li>
            <li>If you export or share files, you control where those files go and how they are deleted</li>
            <li>If you contact support, we keep the message only as long as needed to respond and maintain support records</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            KourtQ is a scorekeeping utility and does not knowingly collect children's personal information through
            a NekoCode cloud backend. Parents or guardians can remove local app data by clearing app data or
            uninstalling the app.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>International Users</h2>
          <p>
            Because KourtQ does not operate a user cloud backend for match data, NekoCode does not perform its own
            cross-border transfers of your match history. Third-party services you choose to use may process data
            under their own policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy when KourtQ, platform requirements, or legal requirements change.
            Updates will be posted with a new "Last Updated" date.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Email:</strong> nekocode.dev@gmail.com</li>
            <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href={`${base}contact`}>NekoCode Contact</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    transition: color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .glass-panel {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  }

  [data-theme="light"] .glass-panel {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    border-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  }

  .legal-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .legal-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 2.5rem;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--color-accent-contrast);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-subtitle {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .last-updated {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .legal-content {
    line-height: 1.8;
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal-content section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .legal-content p,
  .legal-content li {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  .highlight-box {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .highlight-box.primary {
    background: rgba(var(--color-accent-rgb), 0.08);
    border-color: rgba(var(--color-accent-rgb), 0.25);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal-header,
    .legal-content {
      padding: var(--space-4);
    }

    .last-updated {
      margin-left: 0;
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
